<title>UK: Reuters' 3rd ex-UK Asia/Mideast air cargo report.</title>
<headline>Reuters' 3rd ex-UK Asia/Mideast air cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK to the Middle East/Asia GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one. Rates are inclusive of cargo fuel surcharges being applied to airlines.</p>
<p>		    March 7	    Feb 21</p>
<p>			   ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p> LON-BKK	   1.04		 1.04</p>
<p> LON-HKG	   1.20		 1.20</p>
<p> LON-JAK	   1.10		 1.10</p>
<p> LON-MNL	   1.35		 1.40</p>
<p> LON-NRT	   1.95		 1.98</p>
<p> LON-SEL	   1.92		 1.98</p>
<p> LON-SIN	   1.24		 1.24</p>
<p> LON-SYD	   2.15		 2.18</p>
<p> LON-TPE	   1.15		 1.15</p>
<p>		     MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p> LON-BAH	   0.92		0.92</p>
<p> LON-CAI	   0.81		0.82</p>
<p> LON-DXB	   0.80		0.82</p>
<p>		   INDIAN SUB-CONTINENT</p>
<p> LON-BOM	   0.72		0.75</p>
<p> LON-DEL	   0.63		0.65</p>
<p> LON-KAR	   1.05		1.05</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices quoted in sterling per kilo.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel 44-171-542-7706 Fax +5017</p>
